"display_homepage":true,"display_magazines":true,"display_gazettes":true,"display_newsletters":true,"display_noticeboards":false,"display_blogs":true,"display_yearbooks":true,"display_articles":true,"ordering_id":31146,"association":{"type":"article","entity":{"id":"Iz1J2Cr","title":"Complaints Procedure","author":"Administration Manager","show_author":false,"lead":"This guidance document outlines Selwyn United FC\u2019s (<strong>SUFC<\/strong>) process for dealing with complaints and disputes.","body":"<p><strong>Introduction<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>Most often, football in our region goes off without any problems arising and is fun for all involved. However, on the rare occasion, an issue or dispute will arise and you may want the club to assist you with a resolution. You may have had an on-field issue with another team that you feel needs escalation, or you may wish to raise a grievance with the club about a player, coach, club decision, or another matter.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>This guidance document outlines Selwyn United FC\u2019s (<strong>SUFC<\/strong>) process for dealing with complaints and disputes.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>If you are unsure what to do or would like assistance, feel free to get in touch with the General Manager at <a href=\"generalmanager@sufc.nz\">generalmanager@sufc.nz<\/a>. They will be able to help you out or will refer to the complaint to the appropriate person\/body.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>We endeavour to try and find a solution to all complaints or issues that we are made aware of. At the very least, we will endeavour to discuss the issue with you and provide you with more information and\/or assistance. Even if we cannot find an immediate resolution, we still like to be notified of issues so that we are aware of them and able to consider possible change to improve future club operations.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><strong>On-Field\/Football Complaints&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>Most issues that the club deals with are related to on-field events. These may include:<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Improper footballing conduct, for example:<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Inappropriate or excessive pushing\/shoving<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Assaults<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Verbal abuse<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Poor sportsmanship<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Verbal abuse, or inappropriate conduct, from a supporter on the side-line<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Abuse towards a referee<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A player\/team\/referee not properly adhering to the laws of the game<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>In such instances, the first point of call will be to discuss this with your team coach. Usually, coaches will be able to deal with these matters there and then. However, this is not always the case and the club may need to escalate this issue after the fact.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>Should you wish to, you can contact the General Manager at <a href=\"generalmanager@sufc.nz\">generalmanager@sufc.nz<\/a> with your details and a description of what happened. The General Manager will discuss this issue with you and will plan an appropriate course of action. In most instances, these issues are best resolved by raising them with the other club directly.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>If the alleged offender is an SUFC member, then the General Manager will endeavour to discuss the issue with you in the first instance and will then take the appropriate action with that member. This will likely first involve a discussion to ascertain the full picture of what happened, and any resolution will depend on the full context. Depending on the severity of the matter, the club may wish to assist a member with further education or may wish to impose a penalty such as match suspensions.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>Expulsion from the club is a last resort and is generally reserved for the most serious offences and\/or repeat offenders.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>If the response from the other club is unsatisfactory, or if the issue is serious enough, the issue may be escalated to Mainland Football.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Mainland Football Complaints&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>Depending on the severity of the issue, we may wish to refer the issue to Mainland Football for consideration. Mainland Football is the governing body for football in the Canterbury\/Tasman region. SUFC and most of its footballing activity comes under the Mainland Football area of operations.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>In general, the club\u2019s default position is to refer complaints to Mainland Football if they involve:<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; High level physical assaults (for example, a player being punched);<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Serious threats of physical violence;<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Racism;<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \u201cHigh level\u201d verbal abuse; and<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any level of physical assault on a referee.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>While referring any of the above to Mainland Football is the club\u2019s default position, we will seek to discuss the issue with the complainant\/victim before making any decision.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>If a complaint is serious enough or involves a complex issue, it may lead to the complaint being referred to Mainland Football\u2019s Judicial Panel, a group of experienced and independent assessors who will hear the complaint and make a decision on the appropriate action. The Mainland Judiciary has the power to suspend players for a number of matches.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>At all times, Mainland Football and its Judiciary are guided by the New Zealand Football Code of Conduct and make their decisions according to those regulations.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Club Complaints&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>If your complaint concerns a club member or an internal club matter, then these can be referred to the General Manager at <a href=\"generalmanager@sufc.nz\">generalmanager@sufc.nz.<\/a> A \u201cclub matter\u201d may include:<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; An SUFC event or programme, such as:<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Skills\/Talent Centre<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Holiday Programmes<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Summer Football<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Team Selections<\/p>\n\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp; Development sessions<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Junior football or \u201cin-house\u201d football<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Social media posts<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Club communications<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Conduct of a SUFC coach, team manager, player or volunteer<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Conditions of SUFC grounds and facilities (Foster Park, Brookside Park, Selwyn Sports Centre, etc.)<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Sponsorship<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p>If your complaint involves the technical development of a player in our Skills\/Talent Centre or with the technical elements of the programme itself, then in the first instance this issue should be raised with the Director of Football at <a href=\"dof@sufc.nz\">dof@sufc.nz<\/a>. However, the General Manager is also available to assist if required.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Winter Football Administration&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>If your complaint relates to a SUFC-controlled matter, then please see above.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p>If your complaint relates to the organisation of the Mainland Football winter competition more generally, then please note that SUFC has limited influence over these matters. Such an issue could include:<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Scheduling<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Location of matches<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Number of matches played<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Issues with grades, including points tables and promotion\/relegation<\/p>\n\n<p>\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tournament structures<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p>Despite SUFC\u2019s limited influence, please still raise these issues with our Administration Officer at <a href=\"admin@sufc.nz\">admin@sufc.nz<\/a>. They will be able to contact Mainland Football to see if an alternate option can be arranged. In any event, SUFC engages with end of season reviews with Mainland Football after every Winter season and we are able to provide the feedback of our members to Mainland Football directly. If you have raised an issue\/complaint with us, then we may provide this as general feedback so that Mainland Football can implement change in the future if appropriate.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Disputes with the Board&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>If your complaint involves a Board decision or the actions of a club employee (General Manager, Director of Football, Football Development Officer, Administration Officer, etc.) then the first point of contact is the Club President at <a href=\"pres@sufc.nz\">pres@sufc.nz<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>The President will endeavour to assist you with your complaint. Your issue may be discussed at the Board level depending on its severity.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Police Involvement&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>It is rare to have Police involved in community sporting conflicts. However, if the matter is serious enough then SUFC may contact the Police for assistance. For example, if we feel there is a serious and imminent threat to the safety and wellbeing of a person, if somebody has been seriously assaulted, or if any issue involves criminal conduct, then we may contact the Police for intervention and assistance if appropriate.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Conclusion&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>Hopefully, your time with SUFC will be smooth sailing and no issues will arise. However, in any sports club the occasional issue will arise. Should you have a complaint or issue you want to raise then please don\u2019t hesitate to contact us and we will endeavour to assist you.<\/p>","body_mail":"\n        <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>\n        <table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"516\">\n        <tr>\n        <td>\n        <![endif]-->\n        <div style=\"max-width: 516px; margin: 0 auto; box-sizing: border-box; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475569;\">\n        <p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Introduction<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Most often, football in our region goes off without any problems arising and is fun for all involved. However, on the rare occasion, an issue or dispute will arise and you may want the club to assist you with a resolution. You may have had an on-field issue with another team that you feel needs escalation, or you may wish to raise a grievance with the club about a player, coach, club decision, or another matter.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">This guidance document outlines Selwyn United FC\u2019s (<strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">SUFC<\/strong>) process for dealing with complaints and disputes.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If you are unsure what to do or would like assistance, feel free to get in touch with the General Manager at <a ses:no-track href=\"generalmanager@sufc.nz\" style=\"color: #0366d6; text-decoration: underline;\">generalmanager@sufc.nz<\/a>. They will be able to help you out or will refer to the complaint to the appropriate person\/body.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">We endeavour to try and find a solution to all complaints or issues that we are made aware of. At the very least, we will endeavour to discuss the issue with you and provide you with more information and\/or assistance. Even if we cannot find an immediate resolution, we still like to be notified of issues so that we are aware of them and able to consider possible change to improve future club operations.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">On-Field\/Football Complaints&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Most issues that the club deals with are related to on-field events. These may include:<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Improper footballing conduct, for example:<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Inappropriate or excessive pushing\/shoving<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Assaults<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Verbal abuse<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Poor sportsmanship<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Verbal abuse, or inappropriate conduct, from a supporter on the side-line<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Abuse towards a referee<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A player\/team\/referee not properly adhering to the laws of the game<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">In such instances, the first point of call will be to discuss this with your team coach. Usually, coaches will be able to deal with these matters there and then. However, this is not always the case and the club may need to escalate this issue after the fact.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Should you wish to, you can contact the General Manager at <a ses:no-track href=\"generalmanager@sufc.nz\" style=\"color: #0366d6; text-decoration: underline;\">generalmanager@sufc.nz<\/a> with your details and a description of what happened. The General Manager will discuss this issue with you and will plan an appropriate course of action. In most instances, these issues are best resolved by raising them with the other club directly.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If the alleged offender is an SUFC member, then the General Manager will endeavour to discuss the issue with you in the first instance and will then take the appropriate action with that member. This will likely first involve a discussion to ascertain the full picture of what happened, and any resolution will depend on the full context. Depending on the severity of the matter, the club may wish to assist a member with further education or may wish to impose a penalty such as match suspensions.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Expulsion from the club is a last resort and is generally reserved for the most serious offences and\/or repeat offenders.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If the response from the other club is unsatisfactory, or if the issue is serious enough, the issue may be escalated to Mainland Football.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Mainland Football Complaints&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Depending on the severity of the issue, we may wish to refer the issue to Mainland Football for consideration. Mainland Football is the governing body for football in the Canterbury\/Tasman region. SUFC and most of its footballing activity comes under the Mainland Football area of operations.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">In general, the club\u2019s default position is to refer complaints to Mainland Football if they involve:<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; High level physical assaults (for example, a player being punched);<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Serious threats of physical violence;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Racism;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \u201cHigh level\u201d verbal abuse; and<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any level of physical assault on a referee.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">While referring any of the above to Mainland Football is the club\u2019s default position, we will seek to discuss the issue with the complainant\/victim before making any decision.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If a complaint is serious enough or involves a complex issue, it may lead to the complaint being referred to Mainland Football\u2019s Judicial Panel, a group of experienced and independent assessors who will hear the complaint and make a decision on the appropriate action. The Mainland Judiciary has the power to suspend players for a number of matches.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">At all times, Mainland Football and its Judiciary are guided by the New Zealand Football Code of Conduct and make their decisions according to those regulations.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Club Complaints&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If your complaint concerns a club member or an internal club matter, then these can be referred to the General Manager at <a ses:no-track href=\"generalmanager@sufc.nz\" style=\"color: #0366d6; text-decoration: underline;\">generalmanager@sufc.nz.<\/a> A \u201cclub matter\u201d may include:<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; An SUFC event or programme, such as:<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Skills\/Talent Centre<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Holiday Programmes<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Summer Football<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Team Selections<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Development sessions<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Junior football or \u201cin-house\u201d football<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Social media posts<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Club communications<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Conduct of a SUFC coach, team manager, player or volunteer<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Conditions of SUFC grounds and facilities (Foster Park, Brookside Park, Selwyn Sports Centre, etc.)<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Sponsorship<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If your complaint involves the technical development of a player in our Skills\/Talent Centre or with the technical elements of the programme itself, then in the first instance this issue should be raised with the Director of Football at <a ses:no-track href=\"dof@sufc.nz\" style=\"color: #0366d6; text-decoration: underline;\">dof@sufc.nz<\/a>. However, the General Manager is also available to assist if required.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Winter Football Administration&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If your complaint relates to a SUFC-controlled matter, then please see above.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If your complaint relates to the organisation of the Mainland Football winter competition more generally, then please note that SUFC has limited influence over these matters. Such an issue could include:<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Scheduling<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Location of matches<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Number of matches played<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Issues with grades, including points tables and promotion\/relegation<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tournament structures<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Despite SUFC\u2019s limited influence, please still raise these issues with our Administration Officer at <a ses:no-track href=\"admin@sufc.nz\" style=\"color: #0366d6; text-decoration: underline;\">admin@sufc.nz<\/a>. They will be able to contact Mainland Football to see if an alternate option can be arranged. In any event, SUFC engages with end of season reviews with Mainland Football after every Winter season and we are able to provide the feedback of our members to Mainland Football directly. If you have raised an issue\/complaint with us, then we may provide this as general feedback so that Mainland Football can implement change in the future if appropriate.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Disputes with the Board&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">If your complaint involves a Board decision or the actions of a club employee (General Manager, Director of Football, Football Development Officer, Administration Officer, etc.) then the first point of contact is the Club President at <a ses:no-track href=\"pres@sufc.nz\" style=\"color: #0366d6; text-decoration: underline;\">pres@sufc.nz<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">The President will endeavour to assist you with your complaint. Your issue may be discussed at the Board level depending on its severity.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Police Involvement&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">It is rare to have Police involved in community sporting conflicts. However, if the matter is serious enough then SUFC may contact the Police for assistance. For example, if we feel there is a serious and imminent threat to the safety and wellbeing of a person, if somebody has been seriously assaulted, or if any issue involves criminal conduct, then we may contact the Police for intervention and assistance if appropriate.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Conclusion&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Hopefully, your time with SUFC will be smooth sailing and no issues will arise. However, in any sports club the occasional issue will arise. Should you have a complaint or issue you want to raise then please don\u2019t hesitate to contact us and we will endeavour to assist you.<\/p>\n        <\/div>\n        <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>\n        <\/td>\n        <\/tr>\n        <\/table>\n        <![endif]-->","date":"2025-06-01 00:10:00","show_date":true,"editable":false,"location":null,"location_latitude":null,"location_longitude":null,"status":"published","user":{"id":"gGARcL6","first_name":"Administration","last_name":"Manager","avatar_url":"","cw_admin":false,"last_active_date":"2026-06-30 05:16:24"},"created_date":"2025-06-11 00:10:15","updated_date":"2025-06-11 00:25:10","average_rating":0,"attachments":[],"sender_organisation":null,"attributed_article":null,"blocks":null,"default_description":"This guidance document outlines Selwyn United FC\u2019s (SUFC) process for dealing with complaints and disputes....","org_name":"Selwyn United FC","website":false,"shared_to_app":false,"noindex":false,"deleted_date":null,"tags":[],"private_tags":[],"short_gallery":