er":null,"camera":null,"status":"approved","file_150_square_url":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/150x150-a068de11-07ff-4836-b8be-717ffc512e87","file_500_url":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/500-constrained-c5552a9d-fcbe-40ed-a89d-d7e029d3a7e6","file_500_square_url":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/500x500-ebb0a130-951a-4e72-bf21-e1b6a1be9ae2","file_1000_url":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/1000-constrained-25856912-2d28-46f5-9a1b-9ff03e58d4a2","file_1000_square_url":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/1000x1000-3d7b9c41-90d6-4a60-a64a-fcc19dfb05e1","file_2000_url":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/2000-constrained-b323f34a-79e6-481a-8214-fe1e03fa9107","file_original_url":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/original-848c7b15-7f6d-474e-aca3-4c053dd1b86b","original_width":1640,"original_height":924,"focal_point":null,"colour_palette":{"background":{"rgb":{"red":16,"green":0,"blue":93}},"primary":{"rgb":{"red":143,"green":136,"blue":179}},"secondary":{"rgb":{"red":212,"green":209,"blue":226}},"detail":{"rgb":{"red":255,"green":255,"blue":255}}},"tags":[],"private_tags":[],"user":{"id":"gGARcL6","first_name":"Administration","last_name":"Manager","avatar_url":"","cw_admin":false,"last_active_date":"2026-06-30 05:16:24"},"amnesty_expiry":"2024-12-04 03:49:33","created_date":"2024-12-03 03:49:34","average_rating":0,"sender_organisation":null,"attributed_image":null,"noindex":false,"deleted_date":null},"promo4_org_logo":"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/fmgWy6F4toRwkW9hvwbEYe6nzTPbPxt785MgUZgzE0Gkanl9TIGijgwBNqfrWhKP3X9QpUKwx1j4SHQlUbVOkAqAqhaFWGM0cGshziIyatb32PUVm2M5hTPrqu1N0seJ","promo4_link_value":{"id":"RwzIFNn","title":"Selwyn Talent Centre","author":"SUFC","show_author":true,"lead":"Selwyn Talent Centre (STC) provides a year-round program, in conjunction with the school terms, catering for players from the ages of turning 13 years old (in 2026) all the way through to turning 17 years old (in 2026). Players in these groups having the opportunity to represent the Federation at Training Camps.","body":"<p>As well as providing an avenue into the Federations National Pathway and Canterbury Pride set up, Selwyn Talent Centre also provides a direct route into the Selwyn United Senior setup with to date, over 10 current or former Selwyn Talent Centre players receiving their Stallions debuts in the last 5 years.&nbsp;<br><\/p>\n\n<p>Alongside this, we have an ongoing evaluation process which is aimed at giving players the best feedback to ensure they move forward with their development. We also work with other academies during the season to ensure that we have a modern, up to date program that suits our players, and is competitive amongst other training centres in the region.<\/p>\n\n<p>Players set their own standards at the beginning of the season, and each group has an individual attendance target (usually between 80% &amp; 90% depending on the age group). Our aim overall is to be the best on and off the pitch, in relation to our playing style, morals and demeanour.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>Our programme is different to many others as the main aim is to produce great people who can succeed in whatever pathway life finds for them \u2013 not just football!<\/p>\n\n<p><strong><em>What does Selwyn Talent Centre involve and how do I get involved:<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p>Selwyn Talent Centre involves an extra two or three training sessions per week (depending on age level) with OFC B &amp; C Licensed coaches. The sessions have a concentrated focus on tactical development.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>With Goalkeeper Talent Centre, a player would get one specialized goalkeeper session, and one regular STC session (so a total of two extra sessions per week). Spaces within the Goalkeeper Talent Centre are limited as coaches want to keep the sessions as individualised as possible.<\/p>\n\n<p>Any player can look to get involved with Selwyn Talent Centre (you do not have to be a current member of the club). All aspiring Selwyn Talent Centre players get a total of four trial sessions (free of charge). In these trial sessions the coaches would get a good look at the player and how they perform over a longer period of time. A decision would then be made on whether the coaches would like to invite the player into Selwyn Talent Centre, and then with that comes their age group Colts team who play during the winter season and are entered into the youth premier leagues in the relevant age group.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>Selwyn Talent Centre is a commitment, so it is expected that all players commit to Term 1, 2 and 3, with Term 4 being optional. Term 4 is free if your player has done Terms 1, 2 and 3.<\/p>\n\n<p><em>**Please note that all of the Talent Centre and Goalkeeper Talent Centre training sessions are EXTRA, as the \u2018club\u2019 training session is added on during the winter season; so essentially a player in STC would have 3 sessions in total, 1 club session and 2 STC sessions plus a Saturday game (during the winter season and some age groups may have 3 STC sessions per week)<\/em><\/p>\n\n<p><strong><em>The fees for STC and Goalkeeper TC are outlined below:<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Selwyn Talent Centre <\/strong>- $395 per term (remember Term 4 is free if a player completed Terms 1, 2 and 3)<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Goalkeeper TC<\/strong>- $295 per term (GK TC does not run through Term 4 - only 1, 2 and 3, however all GK players would be welcome to train with their STC group throughout Term 4)<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Compulsory Training Kit - <\/strong>purchased by the player and worn to all training sessions, consists of training t shirt, training shorts, pullover, black socks and a bag, approx. cost $235.00 per set.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p>As a club we understand that families will have differing budgets, especially with more than one child playing football; because of this we have a number of payment plan options \u2013 you just have to ask. Mainland football also accepts applications for financial help through the Scorching Goal Fund, and we can assist you with the application process.<\/p>\n\n<p>To register <strong>your interest&nbsp;<\/strong>in having your daughter or son trial for Selwyn Talent Centre please click the link <a href=\"https:\/\/forms.gle\/hP52tJQLAaNcgkm86\">here<\/a>:<\/p>\n\n<p><strong><em>** Please not that this link IS NOT a registration. It is simply just registering an interest. Soon after completing the form you will receive an email with more information.<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n<a href=\"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/2000-constrained-8cf12e5b-d12c-4c2c-a7ab-cf46de5bd540\" class=\"hail-inline\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"text-align: center;\" data-caption=\"\" data-people-html=\"\" data-grapher=\"\" data-width=\"2000\" data-height=\"2000\"><figure text-align=\"center\" data-hail-inline-id=\"Ogq5oxA\" data-hail-inline-type=\"image\" data-hail-width-percentage=\"39.38172043010753\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><div class=\"public-image-wrapper\" style=\"width: 39.38172043010753%;\"><img src=\"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/1000-constrained-e8af43c1-4513-452d-8b57-2ff1f7d8fb00\"><\/div><\/figure><\/a>\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n<p><br><\/p>","body_mail":"\n        <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>\n        <table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"516\">\n        <tr>\n        <td>\n        <![endif]-->\n        <div style=\"max-width: 516px; margin: 0 auto; box-sizing: border-box; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475569;\">\n        <p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">As well as providing an avenue into the Federations National Pathway and Canterbury Pride set up, Selwyn Talent Centre also provides a direct route into the Selwyn United Senior setup with to date, over 10 current or former Selwyn Talent Centre players receiving their Stallions debuts in the last 5 years.&nbsp;<br><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Alongside this, we have an ongoing evaluation process which is aimed at giving players the best feedback to ensure they move forward with their development. We also work with other academies during the season to ensure that we have a modern, up to date program that suits our players, and is competitive amongst other training centres in the region.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Players set their own standards at the beginning of the season, and each group has an individual attendance target (usually between 80% &amp; 90% depending on the age group). Our aim overall is to be the best on and off the pitch, in relation to our playing style, morals and demeanour.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Our programme is different to many others as the main aim is to produce great people who can succeed in whatever pathway life finds for them \u2013 not just football!<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\"><em>What does Selwyn Talent Centre involve and how do I get involved:<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Selwyn Talent Centre involves an extra two or three training sessions per week (depending on age level) with OFC B &amp; C Licensed coaches. The sessions have a concentrated focus on tactical development.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">With Goalkeeper Talent Centre, a player would get one specialized goalkeeper session, and one regular STC session (so a total of two extra sessions per week). Spaces within the Goalkeeper Talent Centre are limited as coaches want to keep the sessions as individualised as possible.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Any player can look to get involved with Selwyn Talent Centre (you do not have to be a current member of the club). All aspiring Selwyn Talent Centre players get a total of four trial sessions (free of charge). In these trial sessions the coaches would get a good look at the player and how they perform over a longer period of time. A decision would then be made on whether the coaches would like to invite the player into Selwyn Talent Centre, and then with that comes their age group Colts team who play during the winter season and are entered into the youth premier leagues in the relevant age group.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">Selwyn Talent Centre is a commitment, so it is expected that all players commit to Term 1, 2 and 3, with Term 4 being optional. Term 4 is free if your player has done Terms 1, 2 and 3.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><em style=\"font-style: italic;\">**Please note that all of the Talent Centre and Goalkeeper Talent Centre training sessions are EXTRA, as the \u2018club\u2019 training session is added on during the winter season; so essentially a player in STC would have 3 sessions in total, 1 club session and 2 STC sessions plus a Saturday game (during the winter season and some age groups may have 3 STC sessions per week)<\/em><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\"><em>The fees for STC and Goalkeeper TC are outlined below:<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Selwyn Talent Centre <\/strong>- $395 per term (remember Term 4 is free if a player completed Terms 1, 2 and 3)<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Goalkeeper TC<\/strong>- $295 per term (GK TC does not run through Term 4 - only 1, 2 and 3, however all GK players would be welcome to train with their STC group throughout Term 4)<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Compulsory Training Kit - <\/strong>purchased by the player and worn to all training sessions, consists of training t shirt, training shorts, pullover, black socks and a bag, approx. cost $235.00 per set.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">As a club we understand that families will have differing budgets, especially with more than one child playing football; because of this we have a number of payment plan options \u2013 you just have to ask. Mainland football also accepts applications for financial help through the Scorching Goal Fund, and we can assist you with the application process.<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\">To register <strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\">your interest&nbsp;<\/strong>in having your daughter or son trial for Selwyn Talent Centre please click the link <a ses:no-track href=\"https:\/\/forms.gle\/hP52tJQLAaNcgkm86\" style=\"color: #0366d6; text-decoration: underline;\">here<\/a>:<\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.6;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold;\"><em>** Please not that this link IS NOT a registration. It is simply just registering an interest. Soon after completing the form you will receive an email with more information.<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n<a ses:no-track href=\"https:\/\/assets.hail-cdn.com\/uploads\/2000-constrained-8cf12e5b-d12c-4c2c-a7ab-cf46de5bd540\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"text-decoration: none; border: none; outline: none;\" class=\"hail-inline\" data-caption=\"\" data-grapher=\"\" data-width=\"2000\" data-height=\"2000\"><figure text-align=\"cent